<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104341" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοπ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for place, in respect to place,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕλη τ.,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ τόπον κινητή</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1042b6
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Peripl.M.Rubr.</u>
					5
				</span></i>
			, al., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.424e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>local,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυλαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					4.14
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνεμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antyll.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				9.9.1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. δυναστεία</span>
			<i>local</i> influence, <i>PRyl,</i><i><span class="en">
				114.16
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. βία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PFlor.</u>
					58.8
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>; <i>of local make,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγγεῖον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>TAM</u>
					2.437
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Patara</span>). Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>
			<i>in the local dialect,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνήθως,</span> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				853 xiii 3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of medicines
			and medical treatment or ailments, <i>to be applied locally,
				topical,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				2.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.383
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. συγκίνησις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					1.46
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροπ-</span> cod.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ἕλκος, πόνος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.36
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fract.</u>
				15
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. διάθεσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					16.710
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ruf.
					<u>Anat.</u>
					30
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.102
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ἐπίρρημα</span> adverb <i>of place,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.T.
				641.32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Conj.</u>
				243.29
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>concerning</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόποι</span> or <i>common-places,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1396b21
			</span></i>; he wrote a treatise <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ
			τοπικά,</span> being (as he says) <i>the method</i> or
				<i>theory of drawing conclusions</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ ἐνδόξων; τ. ἀντίθεσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hermog.
					<u>Stat.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτεροι λόγοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Id.</u>
					2.11
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Stat.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				12
			</span></i>.</div>
